I moved this session to `/Users/hacker/Documents/src/CrackingShells/Murmuration`. The other two sessions on the study folder are idle and untouched. I left its untracked `.claude/` folder and download log alone; they belong to the fork. Both agents treat that folder as read-only.

Wave 1 is running as two Sonnet agents:
- **Platform probes:** a throwaway plugin logs the raw hook inputs from cheap headless `claude -p` runs. It checks, in order of priority:
  - direct messaging between named subagents (the author ↔ verifier pair);
  - which fields SubagentStart and SubagentStop carry for plugin agents;
  - whether `mcp_tool` hook handlers can call a plugin's MCP server;
  - telling your genuine prompts apart from subagent hand-backs and cross-session messages;
  - what the PI agent setting removes from the default prompt.

  Anything only testable interactively comes back as a few-minute manual procedure for you, not a guess. The probe never touches your global settings.
- **Instrument validation:** experiment A replays the surprises from the study's worker reports against the PI notes, checking whether the five known missed signals land where the measures say they should. Experiment B runs two nested Sonnet verifiers on the same claim, one checking independently first and one shown the author's report first, to see whether the pair-independence measures can tell them apart.

Following our own design, both agents were asked to report what puzzled them, with no length cap, alongside their verdicts. I'll read their raw outputs before amending the build nodes.
